This command creates a chart directory along with the common files and
directories used in a chart.

For example, 'helm create foo' will create a directory structure that looks
something like this:

    foo/
    ├── .helmignore   # Contains patterns to ignore when packaging Helm charts.
    ├── Chart.yaml    # Information about your chart / metadata 
    ├── values.yaml   # The default values for your templates ,  for making any customisation to the template [ replicas, resource limit ] 
    ├── charts/       # Charts that this chart depends on
    └── templates/    # The template files ,  collection of yaml files [ deployment, service , cm etc ] that we need to deploy 
        └── tests/    # The test files


